From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jiangcuo <jiangcuo@bingsin.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:54:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] ui/rdp: hand GL scanouts to libvds as dmabufs, share the
 VM between clients

-rdp gl=on lets RDP own the EGL context of GL consoles instead of
-display egl-headless. ui/rdp-gl.c (module ui-rdp-gl, loaded by
qemu_rdp_early_init() before the devices are created) exports every GL
scanout as a dmabuf for libvds' VA-API encoder, so RDP needs no read back.
As egl-headless, the frames are read back into the console surface for the
other displays (-vnc). When libvds refuses the buffer or asks for CPU pixels
(head_input), it is handed that surface; a failed read back keeps the client
on its last frame until the next scanout. Any setup failure only warns and
runs as gl=off. The guest is not held while libvds reads: holding it stalled
dragging in the guest.

With gl=on, RDP starts before -vnc and -spice, as egl-headless does: the
GL consoles they show need the GL context when they register.

-rdp encoder-node=<path> lets VA-API encode on another GPU than rendernode,
the default.

-rdp share=force-shared|exclusive and connections=<n>, as for -vnc: by
default several clients see the display and drive the guest at once;
share=exclusive keeps the previous behaviour. Initialized clients are tracked
by sid.

query-rdp reports share, connections and how each display reaches libvds.

Signed-off-by: jiangcuo <jiangcuo@bingsin.com>
